A44 — fall back to a layout without immutable YCbCr samplers

Binding 4 of the composite descriptor set carries 16 immutable YCbCr samplers.
The Arm driver r38p1 on Mali-G68 (Galaxy A35) accepts the conversion, the
sampler, the set layout and the pipeline layout, and then returns
VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED from vkCreateComputePipelines for every real
composite shader on that layout: 141 of 144 precompiled pipelines fail. The same
BLIT shader compiles with binding 4 declared without immutable samplers, and
trivial shaders compile with the full layout, so the immutable samplers are the
trigger. The failed pipelines were then bound as VK_NULL_HANDLE and the session
crashed.

After the shaders are created, and before the descriptor sets are allocated and
the pipeline thread starts, compile the first precompiled variant (BLIT, one
layer, no YCbCr, one blur layer) once. If it compiles it is destroyed and
nothing else changes, so Adreno and the Mali drivers that already work keep the
existing path. If it fails, rebuild the set layout and the pipeline layout with
binding 4 as plain combined image samplers and write the regular sampler into
those descriptors at dispatch. GAMESCOPE_MALI_NO_IMMUTABLE_YCBCR=1 forces the
fallback layout.

A pipeline that still failed to compile is no longer bound: the bind and the
dispatch are skipped and the missing key is logged (the first 32 times, then
every 600th). The precompile logs its ok/failed totals, and if the first BLIT
variant is still missing gamescope exits with status 86 instead of drawing
nothing. Each failed vkCreateComputePipelines logs the full variant key, and the
device name, driver and descriptor limits are logged once at device creation.

